  "reply": "Thank you for reaching out. I understand you are a hospital looking to use Ledgerly for patient billing and need a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) in place.\n\nAccording to our security and compliance documentation, Ledgerly is **not HIPAA compliant** and **does not sign BAAs**. This means we cannot enter into a BAA with your organization, and Ledgerly should not be used for processing protected health information (PHI) or patient billing that falls under HIPAA regulations.\n\nIf you have any other questions about our data processing agreement (DPA), which is available on all paid plans and incorporates the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, or about our security certifications (SOC 2 Type II and ISO/IEC 27001), I'd be happy to provide more details. However, for HIPAA-covered use cases, we are not the right fit.",
  "sources": [
    "data"
  ],
  "confidence": 1.0
}

